<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis II of Poitiers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1419">1419</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Louis II of Valentinois</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> was the last count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diois">Diois</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley, of the Poitiers family that had ruled there since the 12th century. Childless and in long conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valence">Valence</a> and the house of Savoy, he bequeathed his counties to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dauphin-of-france">Dauphin of France</a>. On his death in 1419 they passed to the French crown despite Savoyard claims.</p></div>
